      "customfield_10012" : "0|i005dz:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "NOTE - this is related to the CancelationToken project - and may just get fixed by that.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Add more docs on canceleation",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "o    SEE if there is some other hack which is more efficient – on POSIX (maybe open ANOTHER bug report for this) – to wakeup for abort case using thread cancelation, or anoter q????",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " OR – maintain linked list of all ‘waitnig’ condition variables (maybe per-thread) – and add/remove when we wiat on condition variable, and in Thead::Abort () – we check that list and send to it (maybe too costly).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "attrs" : {
                        "url" : "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/27341029/what-is-the-best-way-to-wait-on-multiple-condition-variables-in-c11"
                     },
                     "type" : "inlineCard"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "http://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/pthread_cancel.3.html"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "http://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/pthread_cancel.3.html",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "consider using thread cancelation to make ConditionVariable more efficent",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "o    FIX DOCS and implement geter/setter or just document to set the global variables???",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "SO I ALREADY KNEW THIS – SHIT – PACKAGE UP WHAT I HAVE HERE AND USE IN re-use in WaitableEvent. When that works – use THAT in BlockingQueue",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "            public:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "                /**",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "This API shouldnt be needed - if we had a better underlying implementation, and beware, the API could go away",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "bulletList"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "if we find a better way. But callers may find it advisible to control this timeout to tune performance.",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "bulletList"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "                 *",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "The WaitableEvent class internally uses condition_variable::wait_for () - and this doesn't advertise support for",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "bulletList"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "EINTR or using Windows SDK 'alertable states' - so its not clear how often it returns to allow checking",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "bulletList"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "for aborts. This 'feature' allows us to periodically check. You dont want to check too often, or you",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "bulletList"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "effecitvely busy wait, and this checking is ONLY needed for the specail, rare case of thread abort.",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "bulletList"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "                 */",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "                nonvirtual void SetThreadAbortCheckFrequency (Time::DurationSecondsType frequency);",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
